! mcp_bootstrap_p225.strap -- MCP printed page 225: the Input Program's
! boundary-error exit (V BNDER, V BNDMG), the EOJ-scan fixup switch
! (V REX, V REX1, V SREO, V SRE, V SPE2) and V SEOJ .. V EOJ2.
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.232, read at 400 dpi, 900 dpi for
! doubtful glyphs.  Header, READ: "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID
! 11D11MCP  CARD ID 0A000517  DIST. OF 3/01  3/01  PAGE NUMBER 225";
! the heading row's LOCATION field is 224547, line 1's word.
!
! THE PAGE.  52 lines, contiguous from 224547.40 to 224607.00 (a half
! word; next 224607.40).  Lines 16 and 19 are CNOPs that print no
! location and emit nothing.  Lines 17-18 are (A*)DD character data
! (no binary printed): line 17 is 40 characters = 5 words exactly
! (224557.00 -> 224564.00), line 18 is 16 = 2 words (-> 224566.00).
! Remarks run -0521 .. -0562 in DECIMAL (-0537, -0538); -0526 is not
! printed on any row.  Rows 6-10, 12, 16, 20, 22, 25, 41 print none.
!
! GLYPHS SETTLED BY SOMETHING OTHER THAN PLAIN INK:
!  * Line 38 prints "B,V RTIC1": the worn O of p.221's V RTIO1, whose
!    LOCATION 224422.00 is exactly this row's 224422.10 less B's .10.
!  * Line 39 prints "V SECJ", lines 40/44/48 "V EOJ1"/"V EOJ2" with
!    round open glyphs: written O, by line 3's own comment "-CHANGE
!    NORMAL FIXUPS FOR EOJ SCAN" (S EOJ = scan for EOJ).  V SEOJ is
!    referenced nowhere on this page -- rests on the comment.
!  * Line 20 "B,V SREC" and line 24's label "V SREO": one symbol (line
!    20's 224570.10 = line 24's 224570.00 + B's .10); the label's glyph
!    reads as the drum's squared O (same as V REOP on line 22).
!  * Line 43 "V+I,V T2,C": the immediate is 0 -- the row prints
!    000000.15 05 (address 0, J = 6 = V T2); an open round, as in the
!    octal fields.
!  * Line 18's text begins "OUNDARIES": card 17 ends "EXCEEDED B" and
!    the word is BOUNDARIES; the first glyph prints as an open round.
!    Line 18 carries 7 blanks before its "*" (2 words, as line 20's
!    224566.00 requires); measured on the character pitch.
!  * Octal-field opens ("C00000", ".CC", "224557.CC") are 0.  Hex bytes
!    printed with an open round written 0: line 6 "C0" (B,D MCP with no
!    index, as line 25 prints 00), line 36 "BC" (= line 33's B0; p.221
!    line 20 prints the same 031100.02 B0).
!
! CARD SERIALS.  Right-hand serials ?A000517 .. ?A000560, prefix glyph
! read as 0A (same shape p.221 calls DA).  Pairs share a serial: lines
! 6/7 (522), 8/9 (523), 10/11 (524), 12/13 (525), 20/21 (532), 22/23
! (533), 25/26 (535), 41/42 (550).  Asterisks after the LOCATION on
! lines 17 and 32.

